# k < limit with a limit that is any number. Ahead of the loop the limit is converted to a 32-bit integer, and where that is exact the loop compares integers. Another limit takes a copy of the loop that is entered rarely.
# HOT-LABEL: steps by 1
# HOT: Int32 b@{{*}} = BitXor(b@[[k]], $5(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:BitXor)
# HOT: Int32 b@[[next]] = Add(b@[[k]], $1(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:Increment)
# HOT-NEXT: Int32 b@[[goesOn]] = GreaterThan(b@{{*}}, b@[[next]], {{*}}:Less)
# HOT-NEXT: Branch(b@[[goesOn]], Terminal, {{*}}:Less)
# HOT-LABEL: end of loop
# No double lives in the loop: the counter is not converted and the limit is not read as a number.
# NONE-LABEL: steps by 1
